---
title: Content permissions
# Which Discord role may publish what (server/permissions.js). Shown to those
# whose roles include `manage`; the shared admin account always may.
permalink: /app/content/permissions/
tool: content
tab: content-permissions
noindex: true
excludeFromSitemap: true
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
seoTitle: 'Content permissions | AI Safety for Italy'
---
{% extends "app.njk" %}
{% block page %}
    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
        <h2>What each Discord role may do</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="panel-note" style="margin-top:0">Members get what all their roles allow together, read from Discord when they sign in and again before each publish. A role with nothing ticked gives no access to this tool. “Edit others’ content” lets them change and remove items someone else published; without it, only their own.</p>
      <p class="form-note" id="permLocked" hidden>You can change the content columns. The CRM, forms and member applications columns hold access to personal data: only the shared admin can change them.</p>
      <div class="results-wrap" id="permTable"></div>
      <p class="form-note" id="noBot" hidden>The Discord bot is not set up here, so the server’s roles cannot be listed. Add a role by its id (Discord → Server settings → Roles → ⋯ → Copy role ID).</p>
      <form class="form-row" id="addRole" style="margin-top:1rem" hidden>
        <div>
          <label class="form-label" for="roleId">Role id</label>
          <input class="form-input is-compact" id="roleId" required pattern="[0-9]{5,25}">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label class="form-label" for="roleName">Role name</label>
          <input class="form-input is-compact" id="roleName" required maxlength="100">
        </div>
        <div style="align-self:end"><button class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" type="submit">Add role</button></div>
      </form>
      <div class="form-error" id="permError" role="alert" hidden style="margin-top:1rem"></div>
      <div class="action-bar">
        <p>Changes apply from the next sign-in or publish.</p>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" id="savePerms">Save permissions</button>
      </div>
    </div>

<script src="/assets/js/meet/common.js" defer></script>
<script src="/assets/js/meet/app-common.js" defer></script>
<script src="/assets/js/meet/content-common.js" defer></script>
<script src="/assets/js/meet/content-permissions.js" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
